WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:14.870
I’m going to ask you a question and, please,
don’t Google it (or read the title, oh wait,

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:15.870
never mind…).

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:20.080
Anyway, we’re betting that you didn’t
know that Angola was the world’s most expensive

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.080
country…

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.080
Right?

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.080
Come on… don’t lie…

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.060
Well, when it comes to expensive places to
live most people think of New York or Hong

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.270
Kong or Zurich.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.270
Well, that’s not even close to right...

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:35.140
The world’s most expensive city is LUANDA,
the capital of Angola.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.540
And yes, that’s an African country.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:44.420
If you want rent an apartment in Luanda you
can end up paying over $5000 a month.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:47.359
The cost of a Big Mac menu in Maccie Ds?

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:50.199
Yep, that’s 19 American Dollars.

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:52.019
Want to have an internet connection at home…

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:55.280
well you better hope you’ve got a healthy
bank balance, because that’s going to cost

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.949
you around $300 a month.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:57.949
No jokes.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:00:59.769
Alright, so now you might be wondering…

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:02.059
Well, what the hell is going on in Angola?

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:07.410
Is this some extremely wealthy country that
no one knows about?

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:11.729
Well… no.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:15.940
The Republic of Angola is one of the world’s
biggest oil exporters, surpassing other oil

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.940
rich countries like Qatar.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:24.740
Nevertheless, half of its population has no
access to clean water.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:36.770
2 out of 3 kids suffer from malnutrition and
1 out of 6 dies before being 5 years old.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:42.300
Meanwhile, right on the other end of the spectrum,
Angola is the home of one of the wealthiest

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.900
women in the planet, ISABEL DOS SANTOS, who,
by the way, is the daughter of the former

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.890
president, JOSE EDUARDO DOS SANTOS.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:58.360
At this point, you might have figured out
what is going on here...

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.659
Ahh yes, Angola is one of the most corrupt
countries in the world.

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:08.530
Indeed it was home to one of the biggest financial
fiascos in recent years, with several companies

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.150
losing billions of dollars in this country.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.050
Well, perhaps this is no surprise to you…

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:17.829
I mean, at the end of the day, Angola is still
a third world country.

00:02:17.829 --> 00:02:24.540
Nevertheless, there is a question that must
be asked here.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.819
How did they get here?

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:29.480
How could a country possible have such a bizarre
economy?

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.230
And, more importantly, how is it possible
that the ruling party manages to keep control

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.230
of this country?

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:41.480
Well, today, we are going to answer these
questions… but before we do, let’s take

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.569
a look at the history…

00:02:44.569 --> 00:02:46.330
DIAMONDS, BLOOD AND…

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.330
DIPLOMACY?

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.829
The first thing we need to understand when
we talk about Africa is that most of the African

00:02:51.829 --> 00:02:58.400
countries where colonies in past centuries.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:03.469
European powerhouses like Belgium, France
and Portugal invaded most of the continent,

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:09.040
imposing rules and treating the natives like
animals.Angola was no exception.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.260
Until 1975, Portugal made a fortune with its
diamond mines in the country.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:18.680
Nevertheless, in that same year the Portuguese
government, pushed by the UN and its own people,

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.590
recognized Angola’s self determination.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.310
And then the question was…

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.049
What happens after a country stops being a
colony?

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:32.730
Who takes care of the governmental affairs
after the European colonizers leave?

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:39.379
Well… instead of answering to this question
by calling for elections, the many Angolan

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:42.779
tribes created different fronts and started
a civil war.

00:03:42.779 --> 00:03:44.829
This was a conflict that lasted for over 25
years.

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:56.319
Even today, there are areas where you cannot
walk in because they are covered with landmines.

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:57.819
And now you might be wondering…

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:01.019
How is that possible that such a poor country
could afford all those weapons?

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:12.599
Well… the answer there lies in those diamonds
we just mentioned.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:16.810
All sides of the war sold diamonds in exchange
for arms.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.400
But… who provided these?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:23.360
Well, after 1976, when there was a true civil
war, there were two sides.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.750
On one hand, there was the UNITA group, who
dominated the South of the country.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.870
UNITA was supported by South Africa, China
and to a lesser extent, the United States.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.380
Those were the days of the cold war.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.270
Every war in any part of the globe was seen
as a good opportunity to weaken Soviet influence.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.600
Plus, it was known that Angola had oil reserves…

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.360
This also explains why the Soviet Union wanted
to take part in the conflict too.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.810
They supported the Angolan People’s Liberation
Movement, or as they called it, the MPLA.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:57.190
For most of the war, the leader of this MPLA
was Jose Eduardo Dos Santos.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.940
Now Dos Santos did have the support of the
Soviet Union, but, interestingly, the country

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.420
that offered the most support was actually
CUBA.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:15.590
‘We are following our internationalist duty
when we are helping the people of Angola’

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.230
Fidel Castro didn’t stop at selling weapons
to Dos Santos.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.750
He sent over 30,000 troops to the country.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.450
But not only that - during the 1980s, the
area that was under the MPLA control received

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:29.700
a lot of doctors and engineers from Havana.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.070
This explains, partly, why Dos Santos won
the conflict.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:38.000
In fact, despite the war still being ongoing
during the 1990s, this man had taken the control

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.630
of most of the country.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.630
However,

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.080
that Cuban help was not as useful as you might
think.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.150
For example, the agriculture experts sent
from Cuba tried to grow sugar cane on Angolan

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.150
soil...

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:56.300
But, apparently, those seeds were not good
for the kind of soil that you find on Angola.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:06:01.630
And this is why, in just a few years, most
of the farming lands of the country became

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:02.630
totally infertile.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:08.080
That meant starvation for Angolans and anger
towards the Cuban “help”.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:13.380
As if this was not enough, after the collapse
of the Soviet Union, Eduardo Dos Santos realized

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:18.420
that it’s a good idea to befriend the capitalist
countries.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:24.220
At the end of the day, these were the countries
which would but their oil.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.060
On the other hand, America was not helping
UNITA anymore.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:31.570
So, what did this country need to do to become
an ally of the so-called ‘free world’?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:35.470
Well… there was only one thing to do and
that was to remove the word ‘MARXIST’

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:40.220
from their vocabulary and swap it out for:
(sarcastically) ‘FREE MARKET DEMOCRACY’.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:43.960
And yes, I say that with a touch of sarcasm
because Angolan capitalism…

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:51.120
well, it’s certainly one of a kind…

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:53.870
DEMOCRACY, ANGOLAN WAY

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:57.650
Now, the year 2002 was a turning point in
Angolan history.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.840
Eduardo Dos Santos signed a peace agreement
with his adversaries.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.620
Since then, UNITA became a political party,
with a right to run for elections, and for

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:09.030
the first time in history, Angolans could
enjoy democracy.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:13.930
But not only that, in that very same year,
another meaningful thing happened:

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:19.770
“BP makes first ultradeepwater oil discovery
off Angola”

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:25.670
Suddenly, Angola became an oil juggernaut,
selling tons of dinosaur juice to China and

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.840
United States.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:43.990
In just 5 years, Angola multiplied its wealth
by 4.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:48.880
Companies like Exxon Mobile in US or BP in
UK, invested heavily in Angola.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.270
And, of course, they sent engineers and workers
to live in the capital, Luanda.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:58.280
And, of course, these people wanted good quality
houses, cool bars, and the same kind of goods

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.620
they could buy back home.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:03.270
But all those things are hard to find in a
country that, years before, was having a big

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.270
old civil war.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:08.480
In other words: the supply was small and,
yet, the demand wouldn’t stop growing.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:26.070
As a result, the prices for western goods,
went sky high...

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.060
But wait a minute because there’s more!

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:31.780
Imagine we have a construction company in
China and we want to build a housing block

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:32.780
in Luanda.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.969
Well, the first thing we want to do is to
register a company in Angola, right?

00:08:35.969 --> 00:08:38.779
Well, that process can take over 6 months.

00:08:38.779 --> 00:08:42.110
During that time, it’s perfectly normal
that the government finds lots or problems...

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:47.040
They ask you for this paper, that registery,
that other report that you probably don’t

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.040
have…

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.070
You know, the sort of report that a nice stack
of cash, handed to a sweaty palm under a table

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.650
can fix...

00:08:54.650 --> 00:09:01.340
Now, according to several reports made by
organizations like TRANSPARENCY INTERNATIONAL,

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:07.690
almost every company who does business in
Angola has had to do some bribery of a government

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:08.690
official.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.670
But wait a minute because that is still not
the end of it…

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:15.700
Those oil companies like Exxon Mobile or British
Petroleum, who were willing to do businesses

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:21.260
in Angola still had to establish partnerships
with the government or SONANGOL, an Angolan

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.910
state owned company.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.490
And…

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:29.140
now have guess who is the current president
of this company.

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:33.920
Oh, yes, that would be our friend Isabel Dos
Santos, the daughter of the president of the

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:34.920
country.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:41.790
This explains why Isabel Dos Santos became
the wealthiest woman in Africa in so little

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.430
time.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:47.620
Every major Angolan investment held by Dos
Santos stems either from taking a chunk of

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:51.540
a company that wants to do business in the
country or from a stroke of the president's

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.140
pen that cut her into the action.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:57.650
For all this time, the government of Dos Santos,
the father, restricted access to the country

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:58.720
for international journalists.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:03.870
In fact, most of the corruption scandals we
know about have been discovered by the governments

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:09.390
of the UK and the US.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:13.110
Of course, with a political climate like this,
no Angolan wanted to start a company.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.510
At the end of the day, the reality was that
you needed to be a millionaire in order to

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:18.490
pay those various bribes...

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:23.750
And even if we would put the cost of bribery
aside, just with the bureaucracy, you would

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:24.950
need more than $1000 USD

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.180
to start a normal bar in Luanda.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:33.570
In a country as poor as Angola, $1000 is a
fortune.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:34.570
But not only that!

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:39.040
Those international companies were not willing
to invest in the country more than the minimum

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.290
required to extract the oil…

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:44.180
So now you might be wondering: What are the
consequences of all of this?

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:49.000
Well, the outcome is that dinosaur juice is
the only Angolan export.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.370
In the last decade, the only business made
in this country has

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:57.370
been the extraction plants for crude oil and
the home for the company's workers...

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:02.030
By the year 2014, oil represented 97% of Angolan
exports.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:05.170
Does this sound familiar to you?

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:09.370
Well, if you’ve been subscribed to VisualPolitik
for a while, you might

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.820
be thinking about a country with a very similar
economic system.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:14.820
Yes!

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.870
We are talking (again) about Venezuela.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:22.460
Just like what happened on NICOLAS MADURO’s
country, when the oil market price went down,

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:24.260
Angola went right down along with it.

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:27.860
And now, let’s get back to the example of
the Chinese construction companies.

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:32.839
Many firms from China invested millions in
building entire neighbourhoods for expat professionals

00:11:32.839 --> 00:11:33.860
coming to the country.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:50.360
But now there’s no more oil industry and…
therefore, there are no more workers.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:55.440
In summary, there is only one winner in this
story.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:12:00.590
And that person is JOSE EDUARDO DOS SANTOS
and his daughter, ISABEL, who has already

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:03.940
invested those enormous profits overseas.

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:08.830
Most of the big Portuguese firms, from GALP
to UNITEL, are now under the control of this

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.830
family.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:15.210
If Portugal was a colonizer in the past, it
has now become Angola’s money launderer.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:20.490
Angolan elites have sent an estimated $190
billion dollars out of the country.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.060
And, while entire country is having a crisis,

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:27.779
Isabel Dos Santos, who identifies herself
as an “ENTREPRENEUR” on her twitter account,

00:12:27.779 --> 00:12:30.370
goes out with celebrities like Kim Kardashian.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:36.089
All of this being said, you might have guessed
that Dos Santos family is not that popular

00:12:36.089 --> 00:12:39.860
in Angola, right?

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.460
Well, not really.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:47.180
In fact, their political party, the MPLA,
keeps stealing the show election after

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:50.270
election, getting over 70% of the votes.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:56.020
This last August (2017), Angola held an election
and, despite the fact that Jose Eduardo Dos

00:12:56.020 --> 00:13:00.260
Santos was not a candidate anymore, his party
won again.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:02.630
And why does this happen?

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:06.690
Well, I’m afraid we’re probably never
going to know...

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:10.900
‘Angola rejects EU election observers’

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:16.680
And now the question becomes: Can Angola get
rid of this corrupted ruling class one day?

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:17.680
Can they follow

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:20.040
the trend of those African lions like Ghana
or Rwanda?

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:26.640
